# ASTROLABE — the names this product answers for on TLS.
#
# One entry per line:  <hostname>  <address:port>;
#
# The front door is an L4 SNI router: it reads the SNI out of the ClientHello
# and forwards the connection to the address this table names. It terminates
# no TLS, parses no HTTP and holds no certificate, so this table is the ONLY
# thing the two projects share.
#
# The address is where this project's edge publishes 443 on the HOST's
# loopback — the `ports:` in `deploy/edge/compose.yaml`. The two must agree,
# and `deploy/edge/provision.sh` refuses to start if they do not.
#
# Format note: nginx's `map` reads each entry as `name value;`, so the value
# is written as address:port with no scheme and no path — and the trailing
# semicolon is REQUIRED. It is not a nicety: `nginx -t` refuses the whole
# configuration without it, and the front door is what every public name on
# this box depends on. A missing semicolon is a total outage of every name,
# from a typo in a two-line file.
#
# The names in this file are checked against this project's Caddyfile by a
# test, so the front door and the edge cannot disagree about what this
# product serves.
astrolabe.svalley.tech 127.0.0.1:8445;
